# Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com> (2026-08-08)
# ::gentoo masks >=app-text/calibre-8.11.0 (profiles/package.mask, 2025-12-15)
# over the AI features upstream added in that release. The mask has held for
# eight months and pins ::gentoo's installable calibre at 8.9.0, six minor
# series and one major behind upstream.
#
# This overlay ships the current series instead. The AI code is opt-in by
# construction, not by policy: nothing under src/calibre/ai/ is imported until
# the user configures a backend, and Preferences->Tweaks carries
# hide_ai_features to remove the menu entries entirely. Of the seven backends
# upstream provides, two -- ollama and lm_studio -- talk only to localhost, so
# using the feature at all does not require handing text to a third party.
# Nothing here is enabled by default and nothing phones home on its own.
#
# The atom is deliberately UNqualified, which is the opposite of what the
# nodejs entry in profiles/package.mask needs, and for the same underlying
# reason. Portage stamps every repo-level atom with the repository being
# processed, and when it processes this overlay it re-reads the master's
# package.mask too -- so ::gentoo's calibre mask lands here twice, once as
# ">=app-text/calibre-8.11.0::gentoo" and once as "...::bentoo". The ::bentoo
# copy is the one that masks this overlay's ebuild, and only a bare atom
# (which Portage stamps ::bentoo in turn) cancels it. An explicit ::gentoo
# here cancels the wrong copy and leaves 9.13.0 masked -- measured.
#
# Leaving ::gentoo's own calibre ebuilds masked is intentional: this overlay
# ships the version it vouches for and does not unmask a master's packages.
#
# Remove this entry if ::gentoo lifts its mask.
>=app-text/calibre-8.11.0

# Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com> (2026-09-24)
# ::gentoo masked www-client/chromium on 2026-09-24 for last-rites (bug
# #982204, removal on 2026-10-24), citing maintenance cost rather than a
# defect in the package. This overlay has carried its own chromium ebuild
# ahead of ::gentoo's for months (LLVM 22, bin-finder observability, own
# patch rebases) and keeps maintaining it: a from-source Chromium is a
# baseline browser for a distribution, and the ::gentoo alternatives are
# either proprietary binaries or a different engine release train.
#
# Bare atom for the same reason as the calibre entry above: only the
# ::bentoo-stamped copy of the master's mask covers this overlay's ebuild,
# and only a bare atom cancels it. ::gentoo's own chromium ebuilds stay
# masked; they are going away regardless.
#
# After 2026-10-24 the ::gentoo mask disappears with the package and this
# entry becomes a no-op -- remove it then. The chromium-2 eclass is shared
# with google-chrome, vivaldi, opera and others, so it is not expected to
# leave with the package; recheck `inherit` if it ever does.
www-client/chromium

# Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com> (2026-10-20)
# ::gentoo added app-text/podofo-1.1.2 on 2026-10-20 and masked
# >=app-text/podofo-1 the same day (bug #984580): its 1.1.2 goes into SLOT 0,
# replacing 0.10.x under /usr, and the 1.x API is a hard source break for the
# 0.10.x consumers (app-office/scribus, kde-misc/krename).
#
# This overlay's podofo-1.1.2 is SLOT 1 and does not do that. It installs only
# into a private prefix (/usr/include/podofo-1, /usr/$(get_libdir)/podofo-1),
# coexists with ::gentoo's :0 and is picked up only by a consumer that opts
# in -- today app-text/calibre 9.x, which needs the 1.x API. The reason for
# the mask does not apply to it, while the mask itself made calibre 9
# uninstallable on any system that did not already carry podofo:1.
#
# Bare atom for the same reason as the calibre entry above; the slot keeps
# ::gentoo's own SLOT 0 1.1.2 masked, as ::gentoo intends.
#
# Remove this entry if ::gentoo lifts its mask.
app-text/podofo:1
